        "id": "570049",
        "title": "Cookie Combos",
        "difficulty": "easy",
        "description": "<p>In the Cookie Monster Caf&eacute;, the owner wants to showcase the full variety of cookie and topping combinations before rolling out a new menu design.</p>\n<p>You are given two tables: &lsquo;cookies&rsquo; and &lsquo;toppings&rsquo;.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>The &lsquo;cookies&rsquo; table contains &lsquo;cookie_id&rsquo;, &lsquo;name&rsquo;, and &lsquo;type&rsquo;. Each row identifies one cookie and its category (e.g., Choco Chip, Sugar).</li>\n<li>The &lsquo;toppings&rsquo; table contains &lsquo;topping_id&rsquo; and &lsquo;name&rsquo;. Each row names one available topping.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Your task is to determine, for each cookie type, how many unique cookie-and-topping combinations can be made.</p>\n<p>The output columns should be &lsquo;type&rsquo; and &lsquo;combo_count&rsquo;, ordered by &lsquo;combo_count&rsquo; descending, then by &lsquo;type&rsquo; ascending.</p>",
