        "id": "570187",
        "title": "Potion Filter",
        "difficulty": "easy",
        "description": "<p>In the Whispering Woods Apothecary, the potion master needs to spotlight only those brews made with rare roots and update their labels to call them &ldquo;Extract&rdquo; instead of &ldquo;Root.&rdquo;</p>\n<p>You are given two tables: &lsquo;potions&rsquo; and &lsquo;ingredients&rsquo;.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>The &lsquo;potions&rsquo; table contains &lsquo;potion_id&rsquo; and &lsquo;name&rsquo;. Each row identifies one brew.</li>\n<li>The &lsquo;ingredients&rsquo; table contains &lsquo;ingredient_id&rsquo;, &lsquo;potion_id&rsquo;, and &lsquo;ingredient_name&rsquo;. Each row records one ingredient used in a potion.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Your task is to list each qualifying potion&rsquo;s name alongside its core ingredient after replacing &ldquo;Root&rdquo; with &ldquo;Extract,&rdquo; considering only ingredients in the set (&lsquo;Mandrake Root&rsquo;, &lsquo;Wolfsbane Root&rsquo;, &lsquo;Nightshade Root&rsquo;).</p>\n<p>The output columns should be &lsquo;potion_name&rsquo; and &lsquo;ingredient&rsquo;, ordered by &lsquo;potion_name&rsquo; ascending.</p>",
        "schema": "CREATE TABLE potions (\n  potion_id INT PRIMARY KEY,\n  name VARCHAR(100)\n);\nCREATE TABLE ingredients (\n  ingredient_id INT PRIMARY KEY,\n  potion_id INT,\n  ingredient_name VARCHAR(100)\n);\nINSERT INTO potions VALUES\n  (1, 'Elixir of Night'),\n  (2, 'Healing Draught'),\n  (3, 'Shadow Brew');\nINSERT INTO ingredients VALUES\n  (1, 1, 'Mandrake Root'),\n  (2, 1, 'Herb Mix'),\n  (3, 2, 'Wolfsbane Root'),\n  (4, 2, 'Honey'),\n  (5, 3, 'Nightshade Root'),\n  (6, 3, 'Spider Silk');\n\n",
