        "id": "572748",
        "title": "Debate Ratings",
        "difficulty": "easy",
        "description": "<p>The Debate Club partners with a local TV Channel to showcase key matchups. By combining debate scores with broadcast viewership, organizers want to highlight the most intense, high-visibility debates.</p>\n<p>You are given two tables: &lsquo;debates&rsquo; and &lsquo;broadcasts&rsquo;.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>The &lsquo;debates&rsquo; table contains &lsquo;debate_id&rsquo;, &lsquo;topic&rsquo;, &lsquo;home_score&rsquo;, and &lsquo;away_score&rsquo;. Each row records one debate&rsquo;s subject and the judges&rsquo; scores for each side.</li>\n<li>The &lsquo;broadcasts&rsquo; table contains &lsquo;broadcast_id&rsquo;, &lsquo;debate_id&rsquo;, and &lsquo;viewers&rsquo;. Each row logs how many viewers tuned in for that debate.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Your task is to</p>\n<ul>\n<li data-start=\"391\" data-end=\"445\">Consider only broadcasts with at least 5000 viewers.</li>\n<li data-start=\"448\" data-end=\"469\">For each such debate:\n<ul>\n<li data-start=\"474\" data-end=\"545\">Calculate total_points as the sum of home_score and away_score.</li>\n<li data-start=\"550\" data-end=\"584\">Classify the debate&rsquo;s intensity:</li>\n<li data-start=\"591\" data-end=\"621\">'Epic' if total_points &gt; 50, 'Heated' if total_points is between 31 and 50 (inclusive), otherwise 'Normal'.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"721\" data-end=\"752\">Report the number of viewers.</li>\n</ul>\n<p data-start=\"754\" data-end=\"926\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\">The final output should include the columns 'topic', 'total_points', 'intensity', and 'viewers', ordered by total_points descending and then by topic ascending.</p>",
        "schema": "CREATE TABLE debates (\n  debate_id INT PRIMARY KEY,\n  topic VARCHAR(100),\n  home_score INT,\n  away_score INT\n);\nCREATE TABLE broadcasts (\n  broadcast_id INT PRIMARY KEY,\n  debate_id INT,\n  viewers INT\n);\nINSERT INTO debates VALUES\n  (101, 'Urban Planning',     35, 22),\n  (102, 'Economic Strategy',  18, 20),\n  (103, 'Healthcare Policy',  28, 30),\n  (104, 'Cybersecurity',      15, 10),\n  (105, 'Renewable Energy',   32, 25),\n  (106, 'Space Colonization', 45, 15);\nINSERT INTO broadcasts VALUES\n  (101, 101, 5200),\n  (102, 102, 4800),\n  (103, 103, 6500),\n  (104, 104, 1200),\n  (105, 105, 7000),\n  (106, 106, 8200);\n\n",
