        "id": "573665",
        "title": "Flavor Pair Popularity",
        "difficulty": "easy",
        "description": "<p>The ice cream parlor logs all flavors sold within each transaction. Management wants to identify popular flavor combinations purchased together to design new combo offers.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>You are given one table: 'sales': &nbsp;</p>\n<ul>\n<li>The 'sales' table includes the columns 'transaction_id', 'flavor', and 'sale_time', representing unique transaction identifiers, ice cream flavor names, and sale timestamps. &nbsp;</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Your task is to write a SQL query that:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Identifies all unique pairs of flavors sold together in the same transaction.</li>\n<li>Counts how many times each flavor pair occurs across all transactions.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The final output should include the columns 'flavor_one', 'flavor_two', and 'pair_count', ordered by pair_count in descending order and flavor_one in ascending order.</p>",
        "schema": "CREATE TABLE sales (\n    transaction_id INT,\n    flavor VARCHAR(50),\n    sale_time DATETIME\n);\nINSERT INTO sales VALUES\n(1001, 'Vanilla', '2023-07-01 14:30:00'),\n(1001, 'Chocolate', '2023-07-01 14:30:00'),\n(1002, 'Strawberry', '2023-07-01 15:15:00'),\n(1002, 'Vanilla', '2023-07-01 15:15:00'),\n(1003, 'Chocolate', '2023-07-02 10:45:00'),\n(1003, 'Mint', '2023-07-02 10:45:00'),\n(1004, 'Vanilla', '2023-07-02 11:30:00'),\n(1004, 'Chocolate', '2023-07-02 11:30:00'),\n(1005, 'Strawberry', '2023-07-03 16:00:00'),\n(1005, 'Caramel', '2023-07-03 16:00:00');\n\n",
        "slug": "flavor-pair-popularity",
