        "difficulty": "easy",
        "description": "<p>The science fair features student projects across various categories. Organizers require a list of projects by freshmen and sophomores to prepare age-appropriate evaluation criteria. &nbsp;</p>\n<p>You are given two tables: 'projects' and 'students': &nbsp;</p>\n<ul>\n<li>The 'projects' table includes the columns 'project_id', 'project_name', and 'category', representing unique project identifiers, project titles, and scientific categories. &nbsp;</li>\n<li>The 'students' table includes the columns 'student_id', 'project_id', 'student_name', and 'grade', representing unique student identifiers, project IDs, student names, and grade levels (9-12). &nbsp;</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Your task is to write a SQL query that returns all projects with participants in grades 9 or 10. &nbsp;</p>\n<p>The final output should include columns 'project_id', 'project_name', 'category', 'student_name', and 'grade', ordered by project_id ascending and student_name ascending.</p>",
