        "id": "573676",
        "title": "Tournament Dominance Analysis",
        "difficulty": "easy",
        "description": "<p>The e-sports arena tracks team performance across tournaments. Analysts need to identify tournaments where the gap between top and bottom teams is extreme, indicating dominant performances worthy of highlight reels. &nbsp;</p>\n<p>You are given one table: 'tournament_standings': &nbsp;</p>\n<ul>\n<li>The 'tournament_standings' table includes the columns 'tournament_id', 'team_id', and 'total_wins', representing unique tournament identifiers, team identifiers, and their total wins in that tournament. &nbsp;</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Your task is to write a SQL query that:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Identifies all pairs of teams within the same 'tournament_id' where one team has at least 5 more wins than the other.</li>\n<li>Counts the number of such dominant team pairs for each tournament.</li>\n<li>Returns only those tournaments that have at least 3 dominant pairs.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The final output should include the columns 'tournament_id' and 'dominant_pairs', sorted by dominant_pairs in descending order.</p>",
        "schema": "CREATE TABLE tournament_standings (\n    tournament_id INT,\n    team_id INT,\n    total_wins INT\n);\nINSERT INTO tournament_standings VALUES\n(1001, 1, 12),\n(1001, 2, 7),\n(1001, 3, 3),\n(1002, 4, 10),\n(1002, 5, 9),\n(1003, 6, 15),\n(1003, 7, 5),\n(1003, 8, 2),\n(1003, 9, 8);\n\n",
        "slug": "tournament-dominance-analysis",
        "originalCategory": "joins",
