        "description": "<p class=\"ds-markdown-paragraph\">Your best friend Pankaj loves dining out with friends, but as a budget-conscious foodie (₹500 max!), he always struggles to choose the perfect meal combo. Today at \"Duggan's Spice harmony\" restaurant, the server hands you their digital menu table and says: \"Take your time - mix and match to create your ideal thali!\"</p>\n<p class=\"ds-markdown-paragraph\">The 'menu' table includes the columns 'id', 'name', 'price', 'dish_type', and 'like_score'. Each row describes a food item, its price in INR, its category (either 'currie', 'bread', or 'drink/dessert'), and a 'like_score' between 0 and 100.</p>\n<p class=\"ds-markdown-paragraph\">Each thali at restaurant must consist one 'currie', one 'bread', and one 'drinks/dessert' item. As Pankaj's most analytical friend, you pull out your SQL skills to find him the top 3 combos that will:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Maximize taste (highest combined like_score)</li>\n<li>Stay within budget (₹500 total)</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The final output should return the top 3 combinations with the highest 'total_like_score'. If there is a tie, prefer the combination with the lower 'total_price'. If there's still a tie, prefer the combination with lower individual prices in this order: drink/dessert price, bread price, then currie price. <br /><br />The output columns should be 'currie_name', 'bread_name', 'drink/dessert_name', 'total_price', and 'total_like_score'.<br /><br /></p>",
        "schema": "CREATE TABLE menu (\n    id INT PRIMARY KEY,\n    name VARCHAR(100),\n    price INT,\n    dish_type ENUM('currie','bread','drink/dessert'),\n    like_score INT\n);\n\nINSERT INTO menu (id, name, price, dish_type, like_score) VALUES\n(1, 'Butter Chicken', 250, 'currie', 8),\n(2, 'Paneer Tikka Masala', 220, 'currie', 9),\n(3, 'Dal Makhani', 180, 'currie', 7),\n(4, 'Naan', 40, 'bread', 7),\n(5, 'Garlic Naan', 50, 'bread', 8),\n(6, 'Roti', 20, 'bread', 6),\n(7, 'Mango Lassi', 60, 'drink/dessert', 8),\n(8, 'Gulab Jamun', 50, 'drink/dessert', 9),\n(9, 'Masala Chai', 30, 'drink/dessert', 9),\n(10, 'Kheer', 70, 'drink/dessert', 7);",
