        "title": "Chain of Commands",
        "difficulty": "medium",
        "description": "<p>As a senior military analyst, you&rsquo;ve been tasked with mapping the chain of command ahead of a critical strategic meeting. The royal council demands clarity: \"For every General in our forces, trace their loyalty directly back to the Crown&mdash;no ambiguities allowed.&nbsp;</p>\n<p class=\"\" data-start=\"23\" data-end=\"65\">You are given a table: 'army_hierarchy'.</p>\n<ul data-start=\"67\" data-end=\"450\">\n<li class=\"\" data-start=\"67\" data-end=\"450\">\n<p class=\"\" data-start=\"69\" data-end=\"450\">The 'army_hierarchy' table contains four columns: 'id', 'name', 'designation', and 'reports_to'. Each row represents an individual in the army, where 'id' is a unique identifier, 'name' is the individual's name, 'designation' refers to their rank ('King'/'Commander' or 'General') and only three designation are there, 'reports_to' indicates the 'id' of the person they directly report to.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p class=\"\" data-start=\"452\" data-end=\"468\">Your task is to:</p>\n<ul>\n<li data-start=\"471\" data-end=\"527\">Identify all individuals with the designation 'General'.</li>\n<li data-start=\"530\" data-end=\"673\">For each general, trace their reporting structure up to a person with designation 'Commander', and then up to a person with designation 'King'.</li>\n<li data-start=\"676\" data-end=\"761\">Return the names of the general and the corresponding king they ultimately report to.</li>\n</ul>\n<p class=\"\" data-start=\"763\" data-end=\"838\">The final output should include columns 'general_name' and 'king_name', ordered by 'general_name' in ascending order.</p>",
        "schema": "CREATE TABLE army_hierarchy (\n    id INT PRIMARY KEY,\n    name VARCHAR(100),\n    designation VARCHAR(50),\n    reports_to INT\n);\n\n\nINSERT INTO army_hierarchy (id, name, designation, reports_to) VALUES\n(1, 'Shivaji', 'King', NULL),\n(2, 'Sambhaji', 'King', NULL),\n(3, 'Tanaji Malusare', 'Commander', 1),\n(4, 'Yesaji Kank', 'Commander', 1),\n(5, 'Hambirrao Mohite', 'Commander', 2),\n(6, 'Baji Prabhu Deshpande', 'General', 3),\n(7, 'Murarbaji Deshpande', 'General', 3),\n(8, 'Dadaji Konddev', 'General', 4),\n(9, 'Santaji Ghorpade', 'General', 5),\n(10, 'Netaji Palkar', 'General', 1);",
        "slug": "chain-of-commands",
