        "title": "Dual Enthusiasts",
        "difficulty": "medium",
        "description": "<p>In the Vintage &amp; Ice Alliance, managers at the Antique Shop and the Ice Skating Rink reward customers who indulge in both retro collectibles and rink fun. They need a consolidated report of patrons who have rented at least two antiques and skated at least two times, listing the treasures they tried and the dates they laced up.</p>\n<p>You are given two tables: &lsquo;antique_rentals&rsquo; and &lsquo;skating_visits&rsquo;.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>The &lsquo;antique_rentals&rsquo; table contains &lsquo;customer_name&rsquo; and &lsquo;item_rented&rsquo;. Each row logs one rental of a vintage piece by a customer.</li>\n<li>The &lsquo;skating_visits&rsquo; table contains &lsquo;customer_name&rsquo; and &lsquo;visit_date&rsquo;. Each row records one rink visit by a customer.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Your task is to:</p>\n<ul>\n<li data-start=\"454\" data-end=\"569\">Identify customers who have rented at least 2 antique items <strong data-start=\"514\" data-end=\"521\">and</strong> have visited the skating rink at least 2 times.</li>\n<li data-start=\"572\" data-end=\"600\">For each of these customers:\n<ul>\n<li data-start=\"605\" data-end=\"678\">List the rented items as a comma-separated string, ordered alphabetically.</li>\n<li data-start=\"683\" data-end=\"758\">List their visit dates as a comma-separated string, ordered chronologically.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The output columns should be &lsquo;customer_name&rsquo;, &lsquo;items_rented&rsquo;, and &lsquo;visit_dates&rsquo;, ordered by the count of rentals descending, then by &lsquo;customer_name&rsquo; ascending.</p>",
        "schema": "CREATE TABLE antique_rentals (\n  customer_name VARCHAR(100),\n  item_rented VARCHAR(100)\n);\nCREATE TABLE skating_visits (\n  customer_name VARCHAR(100),\n  visit_date DATE\n);\nINSERT INTO antique_rentals VALUES\n  ('Elowen', 'Victorian Cabinet'),\n  ('Elowen', 'Vintage Typewriter'),\n  ('Fiona',  'Retro Telephone'),\n  ('Fiona',  'Antique Mirror'),\n  ('Gareth', 'Old Portrait'),\n  ('Gareth', 'Silver Teapot');\nINSERT INTO skating_visits VALUES\n  ('Elowen', '2025-04-01'),\n  ('Elowen', '2025-04-05'),\n  ('Fiona',  '2025-04-02'),\n  ('Gareth', '2025-04-03'),\n  ('Gareth', '2025-04-07'),\n  ('Gareth', '2025-04-09');\n\n",
