        "title": "Zone Munchies",
        "difficulty": "medium",
        "description": "<p>A crossover event at the Food Truck Park inside the Maze Runner Arena needs to pair runners with the perfect snack trucks. Truck names embed their specialty before the word &ldquo;Cuisine,&rdquo; and participants pick up refreshments matching their run zone.</p>\n<p>You are given three tables: &lsquo;participants&rsquo;, &lsquo;runs&rsquo;, and &lsquo;foodtrucks&rsquo;.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>The &lsquo;participants&rsquo; table contains &lsquo;participant_id&rsquo; and &lsquo;name&rsquo;. Each row identifies one runner.</li>\n<li>The &lsquo;runs&rsquo; table contains &lsquo;run_id&rsquo;, &lsquo;participant_id&rsquo;, and &lsquo;zone&rsquo; (e.g. Taco, Burger, Veggie). Each row logs which cuisine-themed zone a runner tackled.</li>\n<li>The &lsquo;foodtrucks&rsquo; table contains &lsquo;truck_id&rsquo; and &lsquo;name&rsquo; (e.g. &ldquo;TacoCuisine Express&rdquo;, &ldquo;BurgerCuisine Deluxe&rdquo;).</li>\n</ul>\n<p data-start=\"442\" data-end=\"458\">Your task is to:</p>\n<ul>\n<li data-start=\"462\" data-end=\"620\">Extract the cuisine type from each food truck&rsquo;s name by taking everything before the word &ldquo;cuisine&rdquo;, case-insensitive (for example, from &ldquo;TacoCuisineDelight&rdquo; extract &ldquo;Taco&rdquo;).</li>\n<li data-start=\"623\" data-end=\"681\">Match each run&rsquo;s zone value to that extracted cuisine.</li>\n<li data-start=\"684\" data-end=\"807\">Identify every pairing of participant and food truck where the participant ran through the truck&rsquo;s matching cuisine zone.</li>\n</ul>\n<p data-start=\"809\" data-end=\"951\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\">The final output should include the columns 'participant' and 'truck_name', ordered by participant ascending and truck_name ascending.</p>",
        "schema": "CREATE TABLE participants (\n  participant_id INT PRIMARY KEY,\n  name VARCHAR(100)\n);\nCREATE TABLE runs (\n  run_id INT PRIMARY KEY,\n  participant_id INT,\n  zone VARCHAR(50)\n);\nCREATE TABLE foodtrucks (\n  truck_id INT PRIMARY KEY,\n  name VARCHAR(100)\n);\nINSERT INTO participants VALUES\n  (1, 'Alice'),\n  (2, 'Bob'),\n  (3, 'Cara'),\n  (4, 'Dale'),\n  (5, 'Ezra'),\n  (6, 'Finn');\nINSERT INTO runs VALUES\n  (10, 1, 'Taco'),\n  (11, 2, 'Burger'),\n  (12, 3, 'Veggie'),\n  (13, 4, 'Taco'),\n  (14, 5, 'Burger'),\n  (15, 6, 'Taco');\nINSERT INTO foodtrucks VALUES\n  (100, 'TacoCuisine Express'),\n  (101, 'BurgerCuisine Deluxe'),\n  (102, 'VeggieCuisine Cart'),\n  (103, 'TacoCuisine Mobile'),\n  (104, 'BurgerCuisine Wagon');\n\n",
