        "id": "569703",
        "title": "To Be an Engineer",
        "difficulty": "hard",
        "description": "<p class=\"ds-markdown-paragraph\">Behind every aspiring indian engineer&rsquo;s dream lies a critical calculation&mdash;the Mains Entrance Examination ranking system that decides who enters India&rsquo;s premier engineering institutes. The National Agency&rsquo;s algorithm must precisely transform raw exam scores into percentiles, then ranks, and finally, the coveted top 20% who will shape tomorrow&rsquo;s innovations.</p>\n<p class=\"ds-markdown-paragraph\">The examination records revealed:</p>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"ds-markdown-paragraph\">The 'shifts' table contains the columns 'shift_id', 'name', and 'date'. Each row represents an exam shift.</li>\n<li class=\"ds-markdown-paragraph\">The 'result' table contains the columns 'student_id', 'student_name', 'math_score', 'physics_score', 'chemistry_score', 'DOB', and 'examdate'. Each row represents a student's exam performance.</li>\n</ul>\n<p class=\"ds-markdown-paragraph\">The challenge was complex but precise:</p>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"ds-markdown-paragraph\">Calculate four percentiles for each student:\n<ul>\n<li class=\"ds-markdown-paragraph\">Total percentile: based on sum of all three subjects (math + physics + chemistry)</li>\n<li class=\"ds-markdown-paragraph\">Math percentile: based only on math_score</li>\n<li class=\"ds-markdown-paragraph\">Physics percentile: based only on physics_score</li>\n<li class=\"ds-markdown-paragraph\">Chemistry percentile: based only on chemistry_score</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Using the formula for each respective percentile:<br />\n<ul>\n<li>percentile = (Number of same-shift candidates with respective score &le; student's respective score) / (Total same-shift candidates) &times; 100</li>\n<li>All percentiles must be rounded to 4 decimal places</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"ds-markdown-paragraph\">Rank all students using these ordered criteria:\n<ul>\n<li>Higher Total Percentile</li>\n<li>Higher Math Percentile</li>\n<li>Higher Physics Percentile&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Higher Chemistry Percentile</li>\n<li class=\"ds-markdown-paragraph\">Older age (earlier DOB first)</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"ds-markdown-paragraph\">Return only the top 20% of ranked students (using CEIL rounding)</li>\n</ul>\n<p class=\"ds-markdown-paragraph\">The final output should include columns 'student_id', 'total_percentile', 'math_percentile', 'physics_percentile', 'chemistry_percentile', 'student_name' and 'student_rank', ordered by 'student_rank' in ascending order and student_name in ascending order</p>",
        "schema": "CREATE TABLE shifts (\n  shift_id    INT PRIMARY KEY,\n  name        VARCHAR(20),\n  date        DATE\n);\n\nCREATE TABLE result (\n  student_id       INT PRIMARY KEY,\n  student_name     VARCHAR(100),\n  math_score       INT,\n  physics_score    INT,\n  chemistry_score  INT,\n  DOB              DATE,\n  examdate         DATE\n);\n\n\nINSERT INTO shifts (shift_id, name, date) VALUES\n(1, 'Morning Shift', '2025-04-06');\n\n\nINSERT INTO result (student_id, student_name, math_score, physics_score, chemistry_score, DOB, examdate) VALUES\n(101, 'Arjun Mehta',         95, 92, 95, '2005-03-15', '2025-04-06'),\n(102, 'Sneha Reddy',         91, 93, 95, '2005-07-22', '2025-04-06'),\n(103, 'Ravi Sharma',         89, 85, 90, '2004-12-03', '2025-04-06'),\n(104, 'Nidhi Verma',         91, 91, 91, '2005-11-11', '2025-04-06'),\n(105, 'Vikas Patil',         82, 93, 85, '2005-02-01', '2025-04-06'),\n(106, 'Meera Joshi',         76, 80, 78, '2005-08-09', '2025-04-06'),\n(107, 'Ishaan Roy',          70, 65, 72, '2006-01-18', '2025-04-06'),\n(108, 'Priya Nair',          66, 60, 62, '2005-10-05', '2025-04-06'),\n(109, 'Manav Ghosh',         60, 65, 64, '2004-11-30', '2025-04-06'),\n(110, 'Sana Khan',           58, 55, 53, '2005-04-28', '2025-04-06'),\n(111, 'Kunal Yadav',         49, 47, 50, '2005-09-19', '2025-04-06'),\n(112, 'Divya Deshmukh',      45, 42, 40, '2004-08-23', '2025-04-06'),\n(113, 'Zaid Sheikh',         38, 36, 39, '2006-03-03', '2025-04-06'),\n(114, 'Ayesha Mirza',        30, 28, 35, '2005-06-06', '2025-04-06'),\n(115, 'Ayesha Mirza',        28, 27, 38, '2004-03-16', '2025-04-06'),\n(116, 'Ayesha Mirza',        39, 29, 19, '2005-02-12', '2025-04-06');",
