        "title": "Magical Scroll Madness",
        "difficulty": "hard",
        "description": "<p>In the Wizardry Academy&rsquo;s grand Deciphering Tournament, apprentices collect enchanted scrolls whose text has been jumbled by magical rotations. Each letter in the scroll is shifted forward in the alphabet by a specific amount unique to that letter. Your task is to decode these spells so the Council can verify their authenticity.</p>\n<p>You are given two tables: &lsquo;rotations&rsquo; and &lsquo;scrolls&rsquo;.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>The &lsquo;rotations&rsquo; table contains &lsquo;alphabet&rsquo; and &lsquo;count&rsquo;. Each row maps one uppercase letter to the number of positions it&rsquo;s been shifted.</li>\n<li>The &lsquo;scrolls&rsquo; table contains &lsquo;scroll_id&rsquo; and &lsquo;text&rsquo;. Each row holds an uppercase string representing the encrypted spell.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Your task is to:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Split each scroll&rsquo;s text into characters in order</li>\n<li>For each character, look up its rotation count, shift it forward (wrapping Z&rarr;A) to find the original letter</li>\n<li>Reassemble and return the decoded text for each scroll</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The output columns should be &lsquo;scroll_id&rsquo; and &lsquo;decoded_text&rsquo;, ordered by &lsquo;scroll_id&rsquo; ascending.</p>",
        "schema": "CREATE TABLE rotations (\n  alphabet CHAR(1),\n  count INT\n);\nCREATE TABLE scrolls (\n  scroll_id INT PRIMARY KEY,\n  text VARCHAR(100)\n);\nINSERT INTO rotations VALUES\n  ('H',4),('E',5),('L',7),('O',2),('W',3),('R',1),('D',9);\nINSERT INTO scrolls VALUES\n  (101, 'HELLO'),\n  (102, 'WORLD'),\n  (103, 'HELLOWORLD'),\n  (104, 'LORD');\n\n",
