        "title": "Chef Battle Analysis",
        "difficulty": "hard",
        "description": "<p>In the Chef Academy video game, players compete in culinary battles where ingredient access and dish complexity determine rankings. Recent tournaments introduced secret ingredients that alter battle dynamics. Compare chefs who exclusively used these special ingredients in consecutive battles, analyzing their performance shifts.</p>\n<p>You are given two tables: 'chefs' and 'battles': &nbsp;</p>\n<ul>\n<li>The 'chefs' table contains columns 'chef_id', 'chef_name', and 'specialty', representing unique competitor identifiers, gamer tags, and culinary expertise (like Sushi or Pastry). &nbsp;</li>\n<li>The 'battles' table contains columns 'battle_id', 'chef_id', 'ingredient_used', 'score', and 'battle_date', representing challenge identifiers, the participating chef, ingredient name, performance rating (0-100), and competition date.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Your task is to write a SQL query that: &nbsp;</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Exclude any battles where the 'ingredient_used' is common aka ingredient name begins with the word &ldquo;common&rdquo; (case-insensitive).</li>\n<li>For each remaining battle, compute the difference between that battle&rsquo;s 'score' and the chef&rsquo;s immediately preceding battle score. If no prior battle exists, treat the previous score as 0.</li>\n<li>For each chef, identify the single battle that produced the largest positive score difference. If multiple battles tie on difference, select the most recent one.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The final output should include columns 'chef_name', 'previous_score', 'latest_score', and 'score_difference', ordered by score_difference in descending order and chef_name in ascending order.</p>",
        "schema": "CREATE TABLE chefs (\n    chef_id INT PRIMARY KEY,\n    chef_name VARCHAR(50),\n    specialty VARCHAR(50)\n);\nINSERT INTO chefs VALUES \n(1, 'FlameMaster', 'Grilling'),\n(2, 'IceWhisperer', 'Desserts'),\n(3, 'SpiceSage', 'Curries');\n\nCREATE TABLE battles (\n    battle_id INT PRIMARY KEY,\n    chef_id INT,\n    ingredient_used VARCHAR(50),\n    score INT,\n    battle_date DATE\n);\nINSERT INTO battles VALUES \n(101, 1, 'Dragon Pepper', 85, '2023-11-05'),\n(102, 1, 'Common Salt', 78, '2023-11-12'),\n(103, 1, 'Phoenix Shard', 92, '2023-11-19'),\n(104, 2, 'Moon Berry', 88, '2023-11-08'),\n(105, 3, 'Common Oil', 70, '2023-11-10');\n\n",
        "slug": "chef-battle-analysis",
