        "id": "572974",
        "title": "Asteroid Ore Analysis",
        "difficulty": "hard",
        "description": "<p>Space mining operations on distant asteroids require precise equipment coordination. Recent anomalies caused ore extraction discrepancies between consecutive shifts. Investigate equipment pairs used in back-to-back shifts that extracted ore from asteroids sharing a core mineral type, focusing on significant yield fluctuations.</p>\n<p>You are given three tables: 'shifts', 'equipment', and 'extractions': &nbsp;</p>\n<ul>\n<li>The 'shifts' table contains columns 'shift_id', 'miner_id', and 'asteroid_id', representing unique shift identifiers, assigned miner, and asteroid being mined. &nbsp;</li>\n<li>The 'equipment' table contains columns 'equipment_id' and 'serial_code', representing unique gear identifiers, encoded serials (format 'TYPE-REGION-MODEL'). &nbsp;</li>\n<li>The 'extractions' table contains columns 'extraction_id', 'shift_id', 'equipment_id', and 'ore_yield', representing unique extraction events, associated shift, equipment used, and kilograms of ore extracted.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Your task is to write a SQL query that: &nbsp;</p>\n<ul>\n<li>For each asteroid, pair each shift with the very next shift (by 'shift_id') on that same asteroid and for each shift in these consecutive pairs, Compute the total ore yield from 'extractions' table.</li>\n<li>Calculate the percentage increase in yield from the first shift to the second shift:\n<ul>\n<li>percentage_increase= ((second_yield&minus;first_yield)/first_yield)&times;100</li>\n<li>Round this value to two decimal places.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Compare the types of equipment used in both shifts:\n<ul>\n<li>If the equipment type sets are identical and of the same count, label as 'All Same'.</li>\n<li>If there is at least one equipment type in common, label as 'At least one same'.</li>\n<li>Otherwise, label as 'None Same'.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Also, compare the number of unique equipment types used in each shift: If both shifts used the same number of types, label as 'Same Count', Otherwise, label as 'Diff Count'.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The final output should include the columns 'asteroid_id', 'first_shift', 'second_shift', 'first_yield', 'second_yield', 'percentage_increase', 'equipment_type_similarity' 'equipment_count_match', ordered by asteroid_id in ascending order and persentage_increase in descending order.</p>",
